<!-- Application Structure Plan:
    Designed as a modular, non-linear interactive learning experience for new educators. Instead of a passive document layout, the SPA organizes the report's pedagogical core into 6 active modules:
    1. Hero & Mindset Setup: Introduces Adaptive Expertise vs. Tool Hoarding.
    2. Module 1 - What IS AI?: Dynamic visual taxonomy of AI, 5-step machine learning pipeline, and interactive Chart.js Benefits vs. Limitations diagnostic. Includes YouTube video modal integration.
    3. Module 2 - Adaptive Expertise vs AI Workslop: Interactive scenario matrix contrasting Routine vs. Adaptive practice, supported by Cult of Pedagogy podcast listening hub.
    4. Module 3 - Intelligent-TPACK Self-Assessment: Interactive 5-domain rubric with live Chart.js Radar visualization and tailored UNESCO level advice.
    5. Module 4 - Prompt Studio & Roleplay Simulator: Hands-on prompt generator for teachers and live AI parent-teacher conference rehearsal sandbox. Includes Edutopia video guide.
    6. Module 5 - Classroom Ethics & Agreement Generator: Interactive Traffic Light (Red/Yellow/Green) classroom policy generator and Hallucination Detective critical thinking exercise.
    7. Module 6 - Educator PD & Research Toolkit: Curation of agentic research tools, frameworks (UNESCO, OECD), and Substack/LinkedIn networking links.
    Why: Keeps cognitive load balanced, promotes active learning, and provides immediately actionable tools for new teachers.
-->

<!-- Visualization & Content Choices:
    1. AI Taxonomy & Family Tree: Interactive HTML/CSS Card Tabs (AI -> ML -> Deep Learning -> GenAI -> LLMs). Goal: Organize. Interaction: Click tab to update focus block. Justification: Avoids dense text clutter.
    2. AI Benefits vs Limitations: Dynamic Chart.js Horizontal Bar Chart with Category Filter. Goal: Compare. Interaction: Toggle filter between Productivity, Pedagogy, Ethics, Student Impact. Justification: Balanced representation without SVG graphics.
    3. Routine vs Adaptive Expertise Matrix: Dynamic HTML Split View with Scenario Dropdown. Goal: Change/Compare. Interaction: Select real classroom dilemmas to see contrasting responses. Justification: High cognitive impact for teachers.
    4. Intelligent-TPACK Radar Assessment: Chart.js Radar Chart connected to 5 interactive range sliders. Goal: Assess/Inform. Interaction: Drag sliders to see real-time skill profile. Justification: Gives personalized feedback.
    5. Classroom Traffic Light Agreement Generator: HTML Interactive Form yielding formatted printable table. Goal: Create/Organize. Interaction: Toggle green/yellow/red rules. Justification: Provides direct classroom output.
    6. Critical AI Literacy Questions Explorer: Filterable accordion by 6 domains (Output Evaluation, Bias, Thinking Ownership, System Understanding, Ethics, Strategic Use). Goal: Inform.
    7. Video & Podcast Cards: Styled HTML cards with embedded audio player preview UI and links/modal launchers. Goal: Inform/Engage.
    NO SVG graphics used. NO Mermaid JS used. All visual icons utilize standard UTF-8 Unicode characters and CSS design patterns.
-->

